A||N||6||87ECO5||A visit with the previous owner?||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||07-11-2000||08:33 PM||||Well, by the looks of the threads on PFF right now, it appears as if there's a lot of mods being done to the cars in the current Fiero society.<P>Being someone who purchased their car from an owner that didn't have the same feelings for the car that I do (i.e. they weren't a Fierohaulic), I often think about contacting the previous owner to see if they're interested in seeing what I've done to "their" car.<P>Has anyone ever done this?  How did the previous owner react?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||07-11-2000||09:03 PM||||My previous owner runs an auto sales establishment and sold me the car there. He was the original owner and loves Fieros. I've called him twice over the last year with a few questions and he was eager to help, but I remind myself while he's talking...he is a used car salesman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||2
Z||000002||gixxer||07-11-2000||11:42 PM||||HECK NO! The only reason I got my 88 Formula was that it is a perfect candidate for a V-8 swap. When I handed the previous owner her personalized plates back a week after I bought it, all she could do was stare at her "ex" car with gooey eyes, and talk about how much she hated to sell it. It was kinda weird. She also told me she had had it insured for $15,000 because she thought it was going to be a collectable car!(!!!) After I picked my jaw off the ground, I decided not to tell her anything about what I had already done or planned to do to the car. I think it would break her heart.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Boodoggin||07-11-2000||11:53 PM||||I think its a good idea.  Most people who sell thier fieros regret it or at least miss them when thier gone.  They'd be happy to see you've taken good care of it. Im sure they at least wonder about it all the time. Recently I reluctantly sold my GT (long story) to a guy a couple of blocks down.  I stop by all the time just to check it out. He loves it when I stop by just to chat.It was my first fiero and I just want to see it happy. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-12-2000||12:57 PM||||I'd love to rub the previous owners face in it now that it's been cleaned up some and running.  I'm not sure he'd care, though.  He was just a dumb kid who neither knew nor cared what he had.  (WT III can back me up on this.)  Maybe in a couple of years when I get my Eddy Snaauw dash, Ferrari front fascia, Fieroshop hood scoops, and 3.6 I'll email him a picture.  "HA!  Here's what you could have had.  Now it's mine.  All mine!  (You irresponsible little creep.)"<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||07-12-2000||01:52 PM||||Well, some twenty years ago I reluctantly sold my Triumph GT6 (which I had completely restored) to a guy I went to school with that lived a few blocks from my house.<P>After I returned home for the summer from college I was heartbroken to see the car up on blocks with the passenger side front wheel completely mangle.  He apparently ran it into a curb at about 50MPH.<P>||||reg||9
Z||000006||Raydar||07-12-2000||03:03 PM||||The guy who sold me my Formula was the same guy who did the cranberry red Formula with the scoops all over it, and did the 3.4 "from the block, up". <BR>He's (obviously) a Fiero nut like the rest of us. I *don't expect* that he'll have any problem with any mods that I may make.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
